libreac (1.12.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The soname of both libraries is the release version (libreac.so.1.12.0,
    libreac-transport.so.1.12.0), so dpkg ties each program to the libreac it
    was built against; the packages are libreac1.12.0 and
    libreac-transport1.12.0. The ABI promise is gone: LIBREAC_ABI, the layout
    table with its test and generator, and the version ranges that served it.
  * Removed: the append-only enum rule, reac_decode_plain_le, the width-keyed
    reac_ctrl_build_config_announce (use reac_ctrl_build_as with a catalogue
    row), the REAC_ROLE_STATE_APPLIED / _REESTABLISH_PENDING aliases, the
    console_field member name (pace_code), the byte-swapped pcap reader and
    the fallback for kernels older than 4.20.
  * The Python binding loads the soname of its own release.
  * The hardware launch (#64): reac_etf_qdisc_install_offload and
    reac_etf_qdisc_offloaded install and read back mqprio + etf offload, all
    or nothing; the ETF socket carries REAC_ETF_QDISC_PRIO; and
    reac_pacer_launch_stamps_arm / reac_pacer_launch_stamps sample the NIC's
    TX hardware stamps against each frame's launch time.
  * A REAC segment is a physical NIC or a VLAN on one (#65): reac_ifscan
    reads it from sysfs (reac_ifscan_is_physical) and never listens on a
    bridge, veth, tun/tap or macvlan unless reac_ifscan_set_allow_virtual
    names it.
  * The head-amp record is role-blind (#57).
  * rx (#70): update_ppm saturates ppm_error_milli at INT_MAX/INT_MIN and
    refuses a non-finite estimate (0), which no longer bumps ppm_seq; the
    graph clock's ppm_milli (reac_pacer_clock_publish_graph) goes through the
    same saturation.
  * reac_braid_encode (#71) takes audio_len and returns 0 written or -1
    refused (a NULL region, a width not even 2..40, a buffer shorter than
    n_ch * 36) before its first write.
  * reac_frame_ring_init (#72) refuses a request the ring cannot hold: a zero
    or rounding-overflowing slot count, a slot smaller than one frame or wider
    than the u16 length field, or a byte count that overflows size_t.
  * Releases publish to the FreeREAC channel (FreeREAC/freereac.github.io),
    signed by the FreeREAC release key (#79).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0000

libreac (1.11.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ABI break: struct pcap_source gains skipped_oversized, so libreac.so.6
    becomes libreac.so.7 (libreac7). pcap_source_next counts the records
    larger than the buffer it skips, and the capture tools print the total
    (#35).
  * Peer binding: once a box is latched only its own source moves the
    master; the hunt takes a rival into account only after several frames
    over a span; reac_rx drops a frame whose counter is not ahead of the
    last accepted one.
  * The Python binding loads libreac.so.7; fuzz_ctrl's round trip requires
    each block the row has.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

libreac (1.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The etf qdisc read-back (reac_etf_qdisc_state, reac_etf_qdisc_stats_read)
    has a fuzz harness, fuzz_qdisc, over a fake rtnetlink kernel, with 32
    recorded breakages on 7 checks; it is the witness reac-pw's own copy of
    the reader waited for (#8, R3).
  * The dump walker under both reads stops at the bytes recv() returned: it
    compared the remainder as size_t, so an unpadded last message wrapped it
    and the walk ran on into the stale rest of the buffer. Found by the new
    harness; a kernel pads every message, so no rig saw it.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000

libreac (1.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * reac_cfg.h declares the pace and role vocabulary libreac-transport used to
    take from reac-pw: enum reac_rate_refuse, enum reac_role_refuse, their
    REAC_*_REFUSE_CODES_INIT tables, the REAC_RATE_BIT_* and REAC_RATE_ALL_BITS
    masks, and REAC_ROLE_STATE_APPLIED / REAC_ROLE_STATE_REESTABLISH_PENDING.
    reac_pacer.h and reac_role_swap.h include it, so libreac builds without a
    reac-pw header, and the vendored copy of reac-pw's two headers is gone (#8).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

libreac (1.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pcap_source_next skips a record of 0 bytes and goes on; 0 means the end of
    the file and nothing else. It used to return the empty record's length, 0,
    and end the walk on it (#23).
  * The fuzz harnesses are Theorem Labs' per-check rewrite: every property
    check names a one-line breakage and the seed that catches it, 393 records
    on 207 checks, all proven at this commit by `make fuzz-records`, and a
    check without a record is refused. The headers promise what the checks
    hold: a refused decode or scene build leaves its output untouched; the
    scene trailer, the grant sweep's order and head rows, discovery's observe,
    age and JSON, and the head-amp values are documented (#23).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

